      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيَّا آيَةً</span></b> , [inf. n., by rule, as below,] <i>He put,</i>
or <i>set, a sign, token,</i> or <i>mark, by which a person
or thing might be known.</i> (M.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيَّا بِلإِبِلِ</span>,
(inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَأْييَةٌ</span>, Lth, T,) <i>He chid the camels, saying
to them</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيَايَا</span>, (Lth, T, M, and K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيَا</span>,) or
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيَايَهْ</span>, (M,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَايَا</span>, (K,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَايَهْ</span>. (M, K.)

